# `link_table` type tags

Every `link_table` row (and every item in `'links'`) needs `'type'`. The helper prints `[PDF]` (etc.) before the link. **Do not auto-infer** from the URL in `_includes/tables.php`. Uppercase (`'WEB'`, not `'html'`).

| `type` | When |
|--------|------|
| `EXT` | Off-site `http(s)` |
| `WEB` | On-site HTML/PHP, including single-file calculators |
| `DIR` | Folder / directory index |
| extension | File: `PDF`, `TXT`, `KEY`, `DAT`, `JPG`, `PNG`, `XLSX`, `ODS`, … |

```php
// ❌ BAD
['text' => 'ELOG', 'url' => 'https://…', 'desc' => '…']
['text' => 'Notes', 'url' => 'daq/fadc_2010_2012/', 'type' => 'html']

// ✅ GOOD
['text' => 'ELOG', 'url' => 'https://…', 'type' => 'EXT', 'desc' => '…']
['text' => 'Foil heating', 'url' => 'tools/foil-heating/', 'type' => 'WEB']
['text' => 'Photo archive', 'url' => 'photos/', 'type' => 'DIR']
['url' => 'magnets/docs/QM1H02.pdf', 'type' => 'PDF']
```

A one-page calculator is `WEB`, not `DIR`. Nested PHP notes are `WEB`; the listing folder is `DIR`. Missing file type → uppercase extension. `publication_table()` / `talks_table()` do not use these tags.

Sort is by `date` **newest first**, undated last. Do not rewrite array order to “fix” missing dates. Add `'date'`, or `'sort' => false` (written order) / `'sort' => 'date-asc'`. Year archives: each row needs `'date'` plus `'sort' => 'date-desc'`.
